From 8b5ab27a81e46d95a87f4aca100cf2beca213171 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:47:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: check the sold item's own ego for unknown random powers

borg_good_sell() refuses to sell a single unidentified ego item whose
ego type carries a random power, sustain or resist, so that the item is
not given away before that power is known.  The check looked up the ego
of the worn cloak (borg_items[INVEN_OUTER]) instead of the item being
considered.

So a borg wearing a plain cloak and carrying an unidentified Cloak of
Aman next to it treated the Cloak of Aman as safe to sell, and a borg
wearing a random-power ego cloak applied the rule to every other ego
item.

Look up the ego of the item being sold.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#133.
---
 src/borg/borg-store-sell.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-store-sell.c b/src/borg/borg-store-sell.c
index 9fcfd53b3..ceba1f89e 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-store-sell.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-store-sell.c
@@ -918,8 +918,7 @@ static bool borg_good_sell(borg_item *item, int who)
 
     /* Do not sell stuff that is not fully id'd and should be  */
     if (!item->ident && item->ego_idx && item->iqty < 2) {
-        if (borg_ego_has_random_power(
-                &e_info[borg_items[INVEN_OUTER].ego_idx])) {
+        if (borg_ego_has_random_power(&e_info[item->ego_idx])) {
             return false;
         }
     }
